  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Chinar Sheep & Goat Suppliers vs Ut Of J&K & Others on 16 November, 2021",
    "facts": "1 3. The contention of the petitioners in both the petitions is that after coming into force of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 and framing of regulations thereunder, it is not the Department of Food, Civil Supplies and Consumer Affairs but it is the Commissioner, Food Safety, J&K, and the other authorities constituted under the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, who are vested with the power to grant licences. 4. However, during perusal of the record, it was found that only respondent No.3-Director, Food, Civil Supplies and Consumer Affairs Department, has filed reply to both the petitions.",
